1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,831
The disagreement started with a question that nobody wanted to ask: whose body pays for the team's ambition?

2
00:00:06,831 --> 00:00:12,070
“We have a provision for everything except rest,” Daniel said.

3
00:00:12,070 --> 00:00:27,994
“We explain the diet, the play, the condition of the pitch, and the drug rules, and we never mention the actual cost.” His frustration was recent, and it was not only his.

4
00:00:27,994 --> 00:00:32,849
Maya took the other side, and she took it with pleasure.

5
00:00:32,849 --> 00:00:38,009
“Independence means the team sets its own step,” she said.

6
00:00:38,009 --> 00:00:48,218
“Yes, there is a tendency to exclude the slower ones, and yes, the racial history of this sport is a veil over the whole room.

7
00:00:48,218 --> 00:00:57,728
But the preventive work is what we have.” The south end of the field was silent, and the north end was not.

8
00:00:57,728 --> 00:01:05,867
The impact of the argument was circular: the more they attacked the schedule, the more the schedule reacted.

9
00:01:05,867 --> 00:01:21,092
An aggression of small deadlines, a hunger for the next season, and a gun on a poster in the church hall: the frustration of the group was predictable, and so was the optimism of the coach.

10
00:01:21,092 --> 00:01:27,736
The vision of the club had two aspects, and the sight of the two together was tedious.

11
00:01:27,736 --> 00:01:35,196
One was the preservation of a team that could win; the other was the refreshment of people who could live.

12
00:01:35,196 --> 00:01:40,090
“The proverb is right,” the old physiotherapist said.

13
00:01:40,090 --> 00:01:45,090
“A belly full of ambition is still a hungry belly.”

14
00:01:45,090 --> 00:01:52,700
The realization came slowly: the corrective was not a deletion of the programme but a variation of it.

15
00:01:52,700 --> 00:02:03,304
The orbit of the training week had to include the hour nobody trained, and the pleasure of skiing in the winter had to survive the pessimism of the budget office.

16
00:02:03,304 --> 00:02:08,014
“The problematic part is not the plan,” she said.

17
00:02:08,014 --> 00:02:23,797
“It is the uniformity of the people who wrote it.” The hit came from the numbers: frequent injuries, a worse record than the year before, and an intelligence report from the physiotherapist that nobody had read.

18
00:02:23,797 --> 00:02:29,237
“We cannot let one plan prevail over every body,” she said.

19
00:02:29,237 --> 00:02:39,586
They explain the team's own food, the drug rules, and the condition of the pitch, but they never ask who pays at the hour of the training.

20
00:02:39,586 --> 00:02:53,110
The god of the schedule demanded a defense of every hour, and the negation of rest was its poisonous doctrine; a rosy picture through a telescopic lens is still a picture of the foot that hurts.

21
00:02:53,110 --> 00:02:57,159
Give the team its hour back.
